I said it the way I did partly because I enjoyed the opportunity to
use subscripts on poi and ke'a, and partly because it's not clear
which modificands of relative clauses can be referred to within
the relative clause by something other than ke'a.

But, given your user-friendly version, why not go the whole hog:

 *ro da poi da clamau da'a su'e pa ze de poi da .e de remna
